My Express route throws ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT and says it cannot set headers after they are sent to the client. The handler appears to send more than one response.

## What I'm trying to do

I want one request to reach the intended middleware and route exactly once, then produce one predictable response.

## What I've tried

- Added request IDs and logs before and after each middleware.
- Moved the router and parser registration earlier in the application setup.

## Error / logs

```text
Error [ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT]: Cannot set headers after they are sent to the client
    at ServerResponse.setHeader (node:_http_outgoing:648:11)
    at res.json (node_modules/express/lib/response.js:278:15)
```

## Code

```ts
app.use(express.json());
app.use(authenticate);
app.post("/api/example", async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    return res.json(await handle(req.body));
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
});
```

An Express endpoint throws ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT after calling res.json. I think another branch of the route handler tries to respond afterward.

